# each display keeps its own frame age: one caller's frame does not hide a
# change from another. The counts are informative unless damage-exact, so
# the probe tells zero from nonzero only; the calls after the change share
# a block, since printing one counts as a change.
# spec: ADR-1000 platform.multi-monitor
# capability: frame-age-per-caller
size 80 4
cmd frame-since;caller=0
cmd frame-since;caller=1
check
send "A"
cmd frame-since;caller=0
cmd frame-since;caller=0
cmd frame-since;caller=1
check
want test frame-since 0 changed N
want test frame-since 0 changed 0
want test frame-since 1 changed N
